1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:00,420
Oy!

2
00:00:00,720 --> 00:00:01,880
Did you hear that sound?

3
00:00:02,670 --> 00:00:03,520
Oiii!

4
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:07,920
That's the sound oi and oy both make!

5
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:09,220
You hear it in coin...

6
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:10,790
and in toy.

7
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:12,760
Same sound...

8
00:00:12,860 --> 00:00:13,780
different spelling!

9
00:00:15,290 --> 00:00:15,740
So...

10
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:17,670
how do we know which one to use?

11
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:19,780
Here's a simple trick!

12
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:22,940
oi likes to stay in the middle of a word.

13
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:25,820
That's why we write c-o-i-n...

14
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:28,500
coin!

15
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:32,380
But oy likes to be at the end of a word.

16
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:34,750
That's why we write t-o-y...

17
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:37,260
toy!

18
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:39,540
Let's try some more!

19
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:41,240
Soil...

20
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:42,760
point...

21
00:00:44,530 --> 00:00:45,280
foil…

22
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:46,700
oi is in the middle.

23
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:48,400
Boy...

24
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:50,000
joy...

25
00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:51,940
coy…

26
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:53,600
oy is at the end!

27
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:55,920
Now it's your turn!

28
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:57,830
Which one goes here?

29
00:00:58,640 --> 00:00:59,380
enj__...

30
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:01,800
oi or oy?

31
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:05,340
It's oy!

32
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:06,740
Because it's at the end!

33
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:09,460
Now you know!

34
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:12,820
oi goes in the middle, oy goes at the end!

35
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:16,070
Want more fun phonics?

36
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:18,320
Get the English Learning app today!
